course: dictionary
lesson: 5790
title: Macadamia and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A macadamia is a round, creamy nut with a very hard shell. The word can also mean the tree the nut grows on, which comes from Australia. When you read it, look at the words around it to be sure which one is meant.
explain: Macadamia is a noun, so it names a thing. One nut is a macadamia, and more than one is macadamias. «Macadamia nuts» is a phrase where the word nuts tells you which kind of thing is meant.
explain: «Macadamia nuts can make dogs weak, wobbly and sick for a day or two, and nobody knows exactly why.» The clues weak, wobbly and sick show this is bad for a dog. So a food that makes pets ill is one to keep away from them. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A macadamia is a round, creamy nut with a very hard shell.
fact: Macadamia is also the name of the tree the nut grows on, and that tree comes from Australia.
fact: «Macadamia nuts can make dogs weak, wobbly and sick for a day or two.»
fact: Macadamia cookies are popular, so you may see the word in recipes and food lessons.
fact: Some people are allergic to nuts, so always check with an adult before you eat a food with nuts in it.
exercise: What is a macadamia? | A small fish that lives in rivers | *A round, creamy nut with a very hard shell | A hard rock found on the beach | A loud bird that sings at dawn
exercise: «Macadamia nuts can make dogs weak, wobbly and sick.» What does this sentence suggest? | *Macadamia nuts are not safe for dogs to eat | Dogs can fly after eating macadamia nuts | Dogs love macadamia nuts and should have lots | Macadamia nuts make dogs strong and fast
exercise: Which word shows there is more than one macadamia? | macadamium | macadamy | *macadamias | macadamic
test: Which country does the macadamia tree come from? | Italy | *Australia | Egypt | Canada
test: Which word means the hard outer covering of a nut? | tree | creamy | *shell | round
exam: Why should you check with an adult before eating a food with macadamia nuts in it? | *Because some people are allergic to nuts, and a reaction can be serious | Because nuts only grow in the snow | Because macadamias are a kind of fish | Because macadamia nuts are always too cold to eat
